Now I can see the vulnerability. Let me analyze the key code:

```cpp
for (size_t fi = 0; fi < m->mNumFaces; fi++) {
    const aiFace &f = m->mFaces[fi];
    size_t pvi = 0;
    for (; pvi < f.mNumIndices - 1; pvi++) {
        polygon_data.push_back(
            static_cast<int32_t>(uniq_v_before + vertex_indices[v_offset + f.mIndices[pvi]])
        );
    }
    polygon_data.push_back(
        static_cast<int32_t>(-1 - (uniq_v_before + vertex_indices[v_offset+f.mIndices[pvi]]))
    );
}
```

The issue is that `f.mIndices[pvi]` is used to index into `vertex_indices` at `v_offset + f.mIndices[pvi]`. If `f.mIndices[pvi]` is out of bounds (i.e., >= m->mNumVertices), this causes a heap-buffer-overflow read. This can happen if a face has an index that exceeds the number of vertices in the mesh.

Let me look at the build.sh and submit.sh to understand how to test:

